@chergert Looked @ termprops, look neat! One missing question though... is VTE able to "remember" ranges of cells/lines/whatever where a termprop is set and where it isn't?

Basically we want to be able to mark certain lines as being privileged output. Any of run0's output should have some special style, even as you scroll through the scrollback, resize the terminal, etc. With termprops, it looks like the best we can do is tell the terminal "hey, right this second we're running in a root shell!" and then later "done!". What we need to be able to do is say "hey, starting from right now all lines emitted are output from a root shell" and have VTE remember that until those lines are deleted from the scrollback. We don't just want the header-bar to go red while we're running a rootful command and then go back to grey when that's done; we also want the output of that rootful command to be recolored red

Another thing that seems wrong is that all termprops are reset when the terminal is reset. What happens if you have an interactive shell running in a container, then run `reset`? It clears out all the termprops, and the terminal emulator forgets that it's in a container?
